<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Growth Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Organizations often face challenges when attempting to scale product
                    growth. Growth activities can become ineffective when teams focus only
                    on acquisition without improving product value, retention, or customer
                    experience.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Growth Strategy:</b> Growth initiatives without clear
                    objectives can result in disconnected activities. Defining measurable
                    goals helps teams focus their efforts on meaningful outcomes.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>High Customer Drop-Off:</b> Customers may leave during registration,
                    onboarding, purchasing, or other important stages. Funnel analysis and
                    usability improvements can help identify and reduce friction.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Low Product Adoption:</b> Customers may not understand or discover
                    important product capabilities. Better onboarding, education, product
                    messaging, and user experience can improve feature adoption.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Customer Retention:</b> Acquiring customers without
                    maintaining long-term value can make growth difficult to sustain.
                    Teams should continuously improve product experience and customer value.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Insufficient Experimentation:</b> Making growth decisions based
                    entirely on assumptions can increase risk. Structured experimentation
                    allows teams to validate ideas before scaling them.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Growth Without Scalability:</b> Some growth initiatives may produce
                    short-term results but become difficult to maintain. Sustainable growth
                    requires scalable processes, technology, and customer experiences.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant growth challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

