            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Growth Experimentation and A/B Testing</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Experimentation enables product teams to evaluate growth ideas
                    using measurable evidence. Instead of making large changes based
                    on assumptions, teams can test specific hypotheses and compare
                    results against a defined baseline.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Experiments may focus on onboarding flows, product messaging,
                    pricing presentation, feature discovery, user interfaces,
                    conversion journeys, or other areas that influence customer
                    behavior.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Define a clear hypothesis before starting an experiment.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Select a measurable success metric.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Test changes with an appropriate customer group.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Analyze results before deciding whether to scale the change.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Document learnings and apply them to future experiments.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

